## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-5.6 Terra
- **Short description:** OpenAI’s GPT-5.6 Terra is a GPT-5.6 family model positioned to balance intelligence and cost for coding, research, and general professional workloads with a large context window.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API as `gpt-5.6-terra` (per developer docs; also listed for cloud providers). Local metadata lists `openai/gpt-5.6-terra` and `noFreeId` (with Codex quota notes).
- **Release / knowledge:** Release date not explicitly stated in reviewed developer docs; knowledge cutoff February 16, 2026 (OpenAI developer docs).
- **IDs:** `gpt-5.6-terra`.
- **Context window:** 1,050,000 context window; 922,000 maximum input tokens; 128,000 max output tokens (OpenAI developer docs). Local metadata states 1,048,576 (1M).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (OpenAI developer docs). Local metadata lists broader input modalities in text; reviewed official docs confirm text/image in, text out.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $2 / 1M input tokens, $0.20 / 1M cached input tokens, $12 / 1M output tokens (OpenAI developer docs). Long-context (>272K) and cache-write multipliers apply per docs.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary OpenAI model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

